  "body": "223sqm of space. 600m to the beach. Now is the time to make your move.\r\n\r\nPrivately positioned behind secure gates, 61A Vale Road delivers the space, sun and easy living that make St Heliers so desirable - with the village, cafés and beach just a flat stroll away.\r\n\r\nOffering thoughtfully designed living, this is a home that works beautifully for families and downsizers alike, with room to spread out without sacrificing convenience or lifestyle.\r\n\r\nInside, three generous double bedrooms, a dedicated office, two bathrooms, a separate powder room and excellent storage provide flexibility for modern living. The striking double-height living area brings light and volume, while the mezzanine connection to the master bedroom adds architectural character.\r\n\r\nFull double glazing, underfloor heating, a gas fireplace, solar power, quality Bosch appliances and a double garage deliver comfort and practicality. \r\n\r\nRe-clad in 2009, the home also features a Linea weatherboard exterior.\r\n\r\nOutside, established gardens offer a private, sunny setting for entertaining and unwinding, complete with fruit trees and a productive vegetable garden.\r\n\r\nThe location seals the deal. Around 600m to St Heliers Village, Tamaki Drive and the beach, with coastal walks, restaurants and everyday essentials close at hand. Churchill Park, local schools, tennis and bowling are all nearby, while convenient transport links make city access straightforward.\r\n\r\nWith space, privacy and the beachside lifestyle all in one, this is an opportunity worth acting on.\r\n\r\nBE BY THE BEACH, NOT ON THE FENCE. Come and see it for yourself.\r\n\r\nIn zone for Churchill Park School, Glendowie College and St Ignatius School.\r\n\r\nAll conjunctional agents are welcome.",
